All five `tool:medications` turns landed `partial` as expected (the `medications`
tool call returns synthetic `unavailable`; the other five UC-01 tools —
`patient_context`, `problems`, `allergies`, `lab_results`, `clinical_notes` —
and `encounters` still ran for real, so the turn completes with a partial
evidence pack and a withheld claim, not a failure). The `model` fault turn
landed `fallback` (`agent/app/graph/nodes.py:192-193`), matching the same
status every model-backed turn showed in the M4 `--fault model` load-test
control run.

## Alerts evaluator output (`ssh deployer@137.184.4.22 docker compose logs --tail 20 alerts`)

The two most recent lines at the time of this check (10:24:31 UTC, right
after the rehearsal turns) are directly attributable to this rehearsal, not
residual noise from the earlier load test:

```
{"event": "alert", "message": "Tool medications returned unavailable on 100.00% of 5 calls; a service path is broken.", "name": "tool_failure_rate", "rate_window_seconds": 300.4, "severity": "page", "threshold": 0.5, "ts": 1789727071.0817094, "value": 1.0}
{"event": "alert", "message": "5 of 35 clinical tool calls returned unavailable (14.29%); above the 5% page threshold.", "name": "tool_failure_rate", "rate_window_seconds": 300.4, "severity": "page", "threshold": 0.05, "ts": 1789727071.0817094, "value": 0.14285714285714285}
```

`5 calls` exactly matches the 5 injected `tool:medications` faults; `100.00%`
unavailability on that tool triggered the per-tool "a service path is broken"
threshold at `page` severity, the most severe level the evaluator emits. The
aggregate line (`5 of 35`, 14.29%) also crossed the 5% page threshold for
overall tool-gateway health. `35` clinical tool calls in the 5-minute window
is consistent with 5 `tool:medications` turns × 6 UC01 tools + 1 `model`-fault
turn's own 6 tools = 36 expected, within one of what the counter shows
(`Threads_connected`-style windowing/timing at the query boundary; not
material). This is the alerts evaluator's `page`-severity per-tool and
aggregate `tool_failure_rate` gates proving out live, on a deliberate,
controlled fault with a known-exact denominator — as opposed to the earlier
`warn`-severity alert observed opportunistically during M3 verification.

Earlier lines in the same `--tail 20` window are residual `page`-severity
`tool_failure_rate` alerts from the M4 load test (steps 3-4, same day,
~09:34-10:05 UTC) — large call counts (392, 208 clinical tool calls) that
match the load test's real tool-gateway saturation, not this rehearsal.
